Status: PARKED, NOT RULED. Nothing here is built. Budget proposed: 80 lines.
 
## The idea
Incant as a virtual OS: an inverted lookup keyed by field takes the place of a file system. A user (or Clod at recon)
finds a field and sees:
- its description, if it has one;
- what it is (it can be several things at once): registry, rule, incantation, action, command (a field with a C++ method);
- where it is defined (which incantation; can be more than one; file, line, host);
- where it is used, and how: call, attribute or member;
- the statement dresses on it: probe, warning, design-doc link, directive. Each is a field invoked as a field and can be
  switched on and off.
Queries: which actions call this field, or read it as an attribute or member. A search can be limited to the search list
or not.
Readers of the switch: typesetting steps over a statement that is switched off and prints nothing. The jitter skips it too.
 
